<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n105964" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῠρανν-ίς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ίδος</span>,
			ἡ, voc. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τυραννί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>OT</u>
					380
				</span></i>
			:—<i>monarchy, sovereignty,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μεγάλης οὐκ ἐρέω τ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Archil.
					25
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>P.</u>
				2.87
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				11.53
			</span></i> (pl.), <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OT</u>
				535
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ba.</u>
				43
			</span></i>, etc.; of the <i>sovereignty</i> of Zeus, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ Διὸς τ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					10
				</span></i>
			, al., cf. infr. <i><span class="en">
				11.2
			</span></i>:—but more freq. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>despotic rule,</i> obtained by force or fraud, <i>tyranny,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Simon.
				71
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				3.53
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				81
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>V.</u>
				417
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				1.13
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τυραννίδα ἔχετε τὴν
			ἀρχήν</span> (of the Athenians) <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				3.37
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ. ὑμῶν</span>
			<i>lordship</i> over you, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				2.30
			</span></i>: metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ ἐπιθυμιῶν ἐν ψυχῇ τ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					863e
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> in concrete
			sense, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ Διὸς τ.</span>
			<i>royal</i> Zeus, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				345
			</span></i>: pl., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱ τυραννίδες,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ τύραννοι</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				8.137
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἴδεσθε χώρας τὴν διπλῆν τ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ch.</u>
					973
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>territory</i> or <i>resources of a princeling,</i> Liv.<i><span class="en">
				38.14.12
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> fem. of
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τύραννος,</span>
			<i>princess,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Es.</u>
				1.18
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b> name of a
			medicine, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				14.165
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
